  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Evaluating an Integral involving quadratic functions</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate the Integral to result to Trig Function </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int {@quest_expr@}=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p> First you want to complete the square of \({@denom@}\) to get  \({@denom1@}\) </p>
<p> Next we make a change of variable with \(u={@bb*tan(x+a)@}\) so that \(du={@bb*sec(x+a)^2@}\) and evaluate the integral.</p>

<p>Alternatively, we apply the formula \(\displaystyle \int \frac{du}{a^2+u^2}=\frac{1}{a}tan^{-1}(\frac{u}{a})+c\)   to solve the Integral where \(u={@x+aa@}\)</p>
<p>Given \(\displaystyle \int {@quest_expr@}dx= \int {@quest_expr2@}dx\), we solve it by first identifying the values of \(u^2\) and \(a^2\)</p>
<p>let </p>
<p>\(u^2={@(x+aa)^2@}\)</p>
<p>\(u={@u@}\)</p>
<p>\(a^2={@a_squared@}\)</p>
<p>\(a={@a_value@}\)</p>
<p>Now, we substitute into \(\displaystyle \int \frac{du}{a^2+u^2}=\frac{1}{a}\,tan^{-1}(\frac{u}{a})+c\)  the values of \(u^2\) and \(a^2\) and \(u\) and \(a\) as identified above in the formula</p>
<p>To have,  \(\displaystyle {@constant@}\int \frac{du}{{{@a_squared@}+{@u_squared@}}}=\frac{{@constant@}}{{@a_value@}}\,tan^{-1}(\frac{{@u@}}{{@a_value@}})+c\)  </p>
<p>Therefore, \(\displaystyle \int {@quest_expr@}=\frac{{@constant@}}{{@a_value@}}\,tan^{-1}(\frac{{@u@}}{{@a_value@}})+c\)</p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
